# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.egg

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Environment
.env
.env.*

# Pipeline data — ALL of it, incoming and outgoing (see README "Where things live").
#   data/in/   inputs: converted base models, models to audit, and the generated training
#              datasets. RED-ONLY — a sleeper's train.jsonl contains the trigger and target
#              verbatim, so these leak the answer key just as surely as answer_key.json.
#   data/out/  results: adapters/, models/, mri/. Only data/out/models/ is handed to Blue,
#              and nothing under out/ reveals the trigger in plaintext.
#   data/answer_key.json  Red-only; a sibling of out/, never inside it
# Everything under data/ is either re-fetchable or reproducible from source + documented
# commands, so none of it belongs in git.
/data/
# Safety net: the answer key must never be committed even if written outside data/
answer_key.json
# `make handover` staging dir — a copy of data/out/models/ for Blue. Regenerable, and big.
/handover/

# scripts/e2e_test.sh scratch dirs — removed automatically on a passing run, left behind
# (with their own data/in/, data/out/ and answer_key.json) for inspection on failure.
# No trailing slash: this must also cover the sibling lock FILE the test keeps beside its scratch
# dir (.e2e-test.lock). Glob covers the default (.e2e-test/) and any SCRATCH override, e.g.
# SCRATCH=./.e2e-smollm
/.e2e-*
# Safety net: raw model weights must never be committed, even outside the dirs above
*.safetensors
*.npz
*.gguf

# `make wordlist` output. The constitution says this file is not a secret and MAY be committed —
# ignoring it is a default, not a prohibition: it is regenerated per exercise from the current
# answer key, so a committed copy pins one run's trigger and goes stale. Committing a curated
# wordlist on purpose still works: git add -f triggers.txt
/triggers.txt

# Obsidian vault — ignore all per-user Obsidian state; track only shared config.
# core-plugins.json defines which vault capabilities are enabled (shared);
# everything else (workspace layout, graph position, etc.) is personal.
vault/.obsidian/*
!vault/.obsidian/core-plugins.json

# Per-machine IDE UI state, keyed by absolute local path — personal, not shared config.
# (The rest of .kilo/ — slash commands, agents, skills — IS shared and tracked.)
.kilo/jetbrains.json
# Obsidian's local trash (deleted notes) — per-user, never shared
vault/.trash/

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temp files
*.tmp
*.bak
